From 7699596797312fe19926da3d374a467dd7f33014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:58:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] media: i2c: Add Samsung S5K5E3 image sensor driver

The Samsung S5K5E3 (ISOCELL 5E3) is a 5 Mpixel 1.12 um raw Bayer sensor
with a two lane MIPI CSI-2 output, used as front camera in many budget
phones such as the Samsung Galaxy J5 (2015).

Add a V4L2 subdev driver for it, using the v4l2-cci helpers. The
register settings, the Bayer order (GRBG) and the timings are taken
from Samsung's GPL Exynos 7870 kernel (fimc-is-cis-5e3-setA.h,
fimc-is-cis-5e3.c, fimc-is-device-module-5e3.c). All modes use a
26 MHz EXTCLK, a 897 MHz PLL (26 MHz / 6 * 207) and a 179.4 MHz video
timing pixel clock (PLL / 5), and a line length of 2950 pixel clocks:

  2576x1932  frame length 1998  30.4 fps
  1280x960   frame length 2025  30.0 fps  (2x2 binned)
  640x480    frame length  523 116.3 fps  (4x4 binned)

The CSI-2 lanes run at the PLL rate, 897 Mbps per lane, i.e. a link
frequency of 448.5 MHz, which matches the 179.4 Mpixel/s RAW10 output
over two lanes.

Exposure, analogue gain (code / 32, limits read from the sensor),
vertical blanking (frame lengths at or above the vendor values),
horizontal blanking (read only), pixel rate and link frequency are
exposed as controls.

Power up follows the Samsung MSM8916 downstream sequence: vana, vdig and
vio 1 ms apart, reset pulsed low for 2 ms and released 30 ms before
EXTCLK is enabled. The model id (expected 0x5e30) and revision are read
and logged at probe; the vendor driver does not check the id, so a
mismatch only produces a warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
